5,1,1,talk,Asuka,,I need to see the roster books for the late-turn pool and the crew establishment and maintenance contract.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Takumi,,"I want the timed runs and crowd counts mid-city, plus the journey audits on where minutes go.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,I’ll check the capital ledger balances and the ticketing contractor fees. Headlines are useless without knowing the actual long-term commitments.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Servas,,I will examine the two pilots from eight years ago and the completion records of the earlier accessibility programme.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Jonathan,,I’ll look into the joint operators' committee minutes and the contingency pricing inside the pre-war shells.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Asuka,,I’m curious why Jonathan is focusing on pre-war shells. Are we expecting structural surprises that could derail any physical upgrade?,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, are you worried the ground will swallow our plans? I’m just checking if the crowds actually match the complaints.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"I’m watching the money, not the ghosts. If the ledger is hollow, no amount of structural luck saves us from the next budget fight.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Servas,,"The past is a compass, not a cage. I simply want to know if we are repeating old mistakes or finally learning from them.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I’m not chasing ghosts, just the quiet reasons projects stall. Knowing who must agree and what the ground hides helps me trust the dates.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, if the ledger is hollow, we can’t even staff the current routes. I need to know if we have bodies to run the trains before we talk about money.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, bodies matter, but if the trains are empty, extra staff just sit there. I need to know where the actual time goes first.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, bodies are expensive. If the ledger is hollow, we can’t afford the bodies you’re so worried about.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, @Asuka, money and bodies are the fuel, but the map tells us where to drive. We must not confuse the engine with the destination.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, the map is only useful if the road exists. I’m checking if the ground will hold the weight of our promises.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, empty trains don’t solve the problem. If the late-turn pool is empty, we can’t run the service at all, regardless of demand.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, if the pool is empty, we can't run the service. But if the trains are empty, extra staff just sit there. I need to know where the actual time goes first.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, empty trains still burn fuel and require maintenance. I need to know if the money exists before we debate whether the seats are occupied.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, @Takumi, @Asuka, we are arguing over the engine, the fuel, and the passengers, but ignoring the road. Let us see what the past reveals before we commit.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Takumi"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, the road is only as good as its foundations. I am checking if the ground will hold the weight of our promises.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
