35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, the late-turn pool is hollow. Overtime covers everything. We cannot extend hours without breaking the current schedule.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, the data proves the surface route is the bottleneck, not the platforms. We need to fix the mid-city delays, not just add more staff.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, @Takumi, the ledger is ring-fenced, but operating funds are cut. We can’t buy new bodies or fix roads with construction money.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Servas,,"@Asuka, @Takumi, @Benjamin, the past whispers. The late-evening pilot succeeded, and accessibility works delivered. We have proof these paths work, if we respect the constraints.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka"",""Takumi"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, the past is kind, but the present is stubborn. The ferry and rail back offices still haven’t agreed on data terms. That silence will stall any integrated plan.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, the maintenance contract has spare capacity. We can fix the lifts without hiring. But the roster books show no spare drivers. We cannot extend hours.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, spare lift crews don't drive buses. The surface route is the real time-sink. We must fix the mid-city delays, not just the stations.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Jonathan, the data terms are a red herring. The real killer is that ticketing fees now exceed our paving budget. We are bleeding cash on software, not infrastructure.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Benjamin, fees are a leak, not a flood. The pilots proved the late-night model works. We have the proof; we just need the will to act.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, fees are a leak, but unrecorded voids are a flood. Three jobs stalled for weeks. I cannot trust any date involving those pre-war shells.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Jonathan, unrecorded voids are a risk, but empty rosters are a certainty. We cannot build a plan on hope. We must accept the staffing limits.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, certainty is boring. The data says the surface route is the bottleneck. Fix the mid-city delays, not the stations.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Jonathan, voids are a risk, but fees are a certainty. We are bleeding cash on software. I need to know if we can afford the physical work at all.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Jonathan, @Benjamin, risks are shadows, but the pilots are sunlight. The late-night model proved itself. We must not let fear of the unknown block a path already walked.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Servas, sunlight casts shadows. I am not blocking the path; I am checking if the ground beneath it is solid enough to hold our weight.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, spare lift crews don't drive buses. The roster books show no spare drivers. We cannot extend hours.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, you keep repeating yourself. The data is clear: the surface route is the bottleneck. Fix the mid-city delays, not the stations.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Takumi, I hear your frustration, but I am looking at the ledger, not the stopwatch. If we cannot afford the paving, your dedicated lanes are just expensive paint.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Servas,,"@Takumi, @Benjamin, you both see the cracks, but I see the bridge. The pilots proved the late-night model works. We have the proof; we just need the will to act.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Takumi"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Takumi, the stopwatch measures time, but the ground measures risk. I cannot promise a date if the shells might swallow the crew.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
